# Rotate the currently-HELD object through a partial sweep so the camera
# sees it from a few different angles, capturing one frame per step, then
# place it back down at the point it was picked up from. Acts on whatever
# get_object left held — takes no target name because there can only be one
# held object at a time (get_object refuses a second pick while one is
# already held). Refuses (success=false, nothing placed) if nothing is
# currently held. The VLM's inspect_object tool.
---
bool success
string message
sensor_msgs/Image[] views   # one frame per rotation step, in sweep order
string description
